{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own derived deviation block measures the excess on this trip at 7.36 km against an optimal route of 6.4 km, which is 115% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass: the excess is greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms and greater than 20% of optimal. Because it is also greater than 50% of optimal, the deviation is additionally MATERIAL. The governing distance for the threshold test is gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 13.76 km — POL-RD-01 expressly forbids citing the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 13.8 km, and the rider does not rely on it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider has discharged the initial burden under POL-RD-08. The artifacts describe the same trip: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00109, and the pickup/start timestamps agree (accepted 18:17:02, started 18:21:10, first GPS fix 18:21:10). The excess meets the POL-RD-01 threshold on an unimpaired trace — 207 fixes at 10 s intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0. The burden therefore shifts to the driver to name a specific artifact and a specific clause; a general assertion that the rider asked for a stop does not by itself fix the quantum exonerated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-GPS-00109", "EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory exists for this trip. EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING — weight 0.0, issue codes MISSING_ARTIFACT — and carries no payload, so no road, expressway segment or junction can be named under POL-RD-03 as a segment the optimal route traverses. The rider states the impairment plainly: this artifact has no weight and cannot carry a fact, but its absence is citable, and it means POL-RD-03 can exonerate nothing here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00109-01", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider accepts that MSG-00109-001 asks the driver to 'stop at jurong point first' and that the message carries a resolved waypoint_hint at VEN-JURONG-POINT, with the driver agreeing at MSG-00109-002, so POL-RD-04 is engaged. But POL-RD-04 exonerates only 'the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor', and the record contains no computation of that leg: trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null, there is no amendment timestamp for POL-RD-05 to run on, and no derived block measures a detour-adjusted excess. An instruction to make a five-minute stop at one venue does not, without more, price the whole 115% excess out of the claim, and the driver bears the burden of showing the reduced figure he says applies.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the METERED fare the POL-RD-02 arithmetic gives: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 6.4 + 0.28 x 14.0) x 1.0 surge, plus 0.80 platform fee, plus 0 ERP and surcharges, plus waiting_time_fee 0.00, less promo 0 = 12.52 + 0.80 = 13.32. Charged_total is 21.32, so the refund is 8.00. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and is 37.5% of the amount charged, far below the 90% that would convert it to a full refund — so the rider's claim is for a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 8.00. The platform's own fare model reaches the identical figure (refund.payable 8.00), which the rider adopts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was metered time_fare of 9.52 for 34.0 charged minutes against an optimal_duration_min of 14.0, and the fare carries waiting_time_fee of 0.00 — the minutes spent at the pickup point were billed as trip time, not as a separate waiting charge. POL-RD-02 prices the recomputed fare at the optimal duration and then adds fare_breakdown.waiting_time_fee, which here is zero. There is no properly chargeable waiting line to add back into the recomputation, and the rider should not be asked to pay again in the waiting column for time already priced out of the distance-and-time lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The extra corroboration requirement in POL-RD-08 does not bite on this rider. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0 — nowhere near the 4-or-more claims with 1-or-fewer substantiated that the clause names — and the requirement applies only to excesses below 30%, whereas this excess is 115%. The rider's claim also does not rest on assertion alone: it rests on the same platform telemetry the fare was billed from.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The MATERIAL finding under POL-RD-01 requires the driver_profile check in POL-RD-06, and the rider states the result honestly: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 511 — no pattern is established on the trailing-90-day counters, and the rider does not seek the POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift. The materiality finding itself stands on this trip's own evidence, which is all POL-RD-06 permits it to rest on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's statement that he drove 13.8 km while the receipt shows 9.6 km is arithmetically right — distance_charged_km is 9.60 against a trace_distance_km of 13.76 — but POL-RD-04's compensation limb is discretionary ('may be granted'), and if it is granted at all it is a driver payment that POL-GEN-03 makes INDEPENDENT of the rider's refund and never netted against it. It cannot be used to reduce or offset the SGD 8.00 the rider is owed on the mileage and time actually contested.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.15,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the rider's route-deviation claim is not supported, and the driver is owed a small under-billing payment of SGD 3.15.\n\nROUTE DEVIATION. On the platform's own measurement the trip ran 13.76 km (gps_trace.trace_distance_km) against an optimal 6.4 km — an excess of 7.36 km, 115% of optimal. That would clear both POL-RD-01 tests and be a MATERIAL deviation. It is, however, fully excused by POL-RD-04. The chat log carries the rider's own message MSG-00109-001, sent 18:22:06 — 56 seconds after the meter started at 18:21:10: 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min'. It comes from the rider, sits well inside the clause's three-minute window, and names the very place the clause gives as its example. The waypoint the platform resolved from that text is Jurong Point PHV Pickup Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT), and the GPS trace shows the vehicle stationary 38 m from it for 366 seconds — inside the 200 m proximity test. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 207 fixes at 10 s, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0. The whole measured excess lies on that diversion — the vehicle left the optimal corridor for Jurong Point and rejoined it on the run to Bukit Batok — so once the excess between leaving and rejoining is excluded, nothing remains that passes POL-RD-01 and no deviation is established. No POL-RD-02 recomputation therefore runs, and the rider's figure of an SGD 8.00 partial refund (recomputed_fare 13.32 against charged_total 21.32) is the arithmetic of a deviation that is fully excused; it does not issue. The rider's point that the record contains no stored computation of the excluded leg does not change this: POL-RD-05 never engages (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, so no re-quote was required), POL-RD-04 calls for no stored figure, and the trace together with the resolved waypoint shows the entire diversion is the stop she asked for.\n\nDRIVER COMPENSATION. The fare billed the rider for 9.60 km (distance_charged_km) while the trace records 13.76 km — a shortfall of 4.16 km, above the 1.0 km trigger in POL-RD-04. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is 4.16 x 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded UP to SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. The driver is entitled to SGD 3.15. This is a payment to the driver, independent of any rider refund and never netted against one; the rider's own charge stands.\n\nOTHER CLAUSES. POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no payload, though the case does not need it — both advocates disclosed that impairment. POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is clean (deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 511), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral; the claim correctly uses the trailing-90-day counter and does not rely on lifetime prior_deviation_flags. POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct — no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge — and POL-RD-09(3) gives no ERP refund on a rider-caused detour. POL-RD-08's extra corroboration requirement does not bite (deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0, and the excess is 115%, not below 30%). No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is not impaired, trip identifiers and timestamps agree, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing or incomplete artifact, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.15,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The trip did deviate: the optimal route Clementi to Bukit Batok is 6.4 km, the GPS trace records 13.76 km, an excess of 7.36 km, which is 115% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 establishment tests and is MATERIAL, and I accept it. But the deviation is the rider's, and POL-RD-04 excuses it. The rider's own message MSG-00109-001, sent at 18:22:06 — 56 seconds after the meter started at 18:21:10 — reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', and the platform resolved the waypoint Jurong Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT) from that text; the driver agreed at 18:22:31. The GPS trace — complete, 207 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps — puts the vehicle stationary 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds, inside the clause's 200 m corroboration test. The instruction came from the rider, inside the 3-minute window, and 'stop at Jurong Point first' is the clause's own example of a place named specifically enough to act on. POL-RD-04 excludes the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor; the route actually driven is the route to Jurong Point and on to Bukit Batok, so the whole 7.36 km excess is that detour, nothing survives the exclusion, no deviation remains, and the rider's refund is nil. The rider's advocate is right that the raw excess is 115% and MATERIAL, but wrong that POL-RD-02 produces SGD 8.00 here: POL-RD-04 requires the detour excess to be excluded before POL-RD-02 runs, and once it is there is no deviation to refund against. I also reject his submission that the exoneration is unquantified: POL-RD-04 runs on the chat log, the resolved waypoint and the trace, all present at full weight, and the stored amended-route field he points to is POL-RD-05's requirement, not engaged here because no endpoint was amended (amended_optimal_distance_km is null and no amendment timestamp exists). The claimed refund of 8.00 is not made; charged_total 21.32 and recomputed_fare 13.32 are recorded, but the 8.00 difference is the exonerated detour and the charge of SGD 21.32 stands. The waiting-time point is moot: the fare carries waiting_time_fee 0.00, so there is no waiting line to add back. On the driver's side, the fare breakdown bills 9.60 km while the trace records 13.76 km — a 4.16 km shortfall, past the 1.0 km trigger. Under POL-RD-04's separate limb I grant the driver DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 4.16 x SGD 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded up to SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 cap. This is a platform-funded payment to the driver; it is independent of any rider refund, is not netted against the rider, and leaves the rider's charge standing. No traffic advisory exists: EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; its absence is citable and means POL-RD-03 can exonerate nothing, but it carries no fact, and this ruling rests on no impaired artifact. Nothing arises under POL-RD-09: the fare carries no ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge. POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is clean — deviation_flags_90d 0 across completed_trips_90d 511 — so there is no repeat pattern, no uplift to FULL_REFUND and no driver-conduct referral. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and is not a ground of decision; the only surviving claim that mentions it correctly disclaims it. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is complete and unimpaired, the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across trip record, trace and fare, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The case is decidable on the papers. Ruling: DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount SGD 3.15, driver compensation SGD 3.15, confidence 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.15,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The platform's measurements are accepted as they stand: the trip ran 13.76 km (GPS trace EV-GPS-00109) against an optimal route of 6.4 km (trip record EV-TRIP-00109), an excess of 7.36 km and 115% of optimal. On those figures alone the excess is MATERIAL under POL-RD-01. But the excess does not survive POL-RD-04.\n\nPOL-RD-04 applies limb by limb. (a) The instruction is the rider's own: MSG-00109-001 on the chat log (EV-CHAT-00109), 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', sender RIDER. (b) It was sent at 18:22:06, 56 seconds after the trip started at 18:21:10 — inside the clause's 3-minute allowance. (c) It names a place specifically enough to act on, and the clause's own example is 'stop at Jurong Point first'; it carries the platform-resolved waypoint_hint for Jurong Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT), and the driver agreed at MSG-00109-002. The GPS trace corroborates it as the clause requires: the vehicle was stationary 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds, well inside the 200 m proximity test. The whole of the 7.36 km excess is the excursion the rider asked for — the trace distance is the Clementi-to-Jurong-Point-to-Bukit-Batok route, and its excess over the direct 6.4 km optimal is precisely that diversion. Excluding it leaves no excess; both POL-RD-01 establishment tests fail; no deviation is established. The rider's narrative that the driver 'anyhow drove' is contradicted by her own message one minute into the trip and by her 'coming down now' at 18:35:40 after the stop. The rider's waiting-time point (time_fare 9.52 for 34.0 charged minutes against an optimal duration of 14.0, waiting_time_fee 0.00) is answered the same way: the time was her own requested stop, and the fare stands. The POL-RD-02 arithmetic the rider offers (charged_total 21.32, recomputed_fare 13.32, refund 8.00) only runs if a deviation survives, and none does. I make no refund; the charge of 21.32 stands and the contested 12.00 is not supported. The rider's own profile claim under POL-RD-08 (deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0) is accepted and changes nothing.\n\nThe driver is separately under-billed. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) bills distance_charged_km of 9.60 while the trace records 13.76 km — a shortfall of 4.16 km, past the 1.0 km trigger in POL-RD-04. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre, 4.16 x 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded up to SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 cap. I grant DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.15. Under POL-GEN-03 this is independent of the rider's position and is not netted against anything, and on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd carries the same figure.\n\nThe rider's objection that no artifact computes the detour leg does not change the result: POL-RD-04's exclusion runs on the record's own figures, and the amended-endpoint figures the rider looks for belong to POL-RD-05, which has no application because no endpoint was amended.\n\nOn the remaining clauses: the rider's POL-RD-08 identity-and-threshold showing is made out, and the driver discharges the shifted burden with a specific artifact and a specific clause (EV-CHAT-00109 and POL-RD-04). EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING — weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so it carries no fact and POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing; that is immaterial here because the detour is rider-caused, not road-caused. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is clean (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 511), so there is no POL-RD-06(b) uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and nothing rests on it. POL-RD-09 produces nothing: no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge, so no pass-through or billing-integrity correction arises. The trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (207 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, max gap 0.0), so no POL-RD-10(3) escalation and no POL-GEN-02(2) discount is engaged. No escalation trigger fires. Confidence is capped at 1.0 by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (the GPS trace, the chat log, the trip record and the fare breakdown); I record 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
