    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Addressed to both parties.\n\nRider — your route-deviation complaint is not supported, and no refund issues. The trip telemetry does show the raw deviation you describe: the GPS trace records 13.76 km against the platform's optimal 6.4 km, an excess of 7.36 km (115%), which is a MATERIAL deviation under POL-RD-01. But the cause is your own instruction. Your message MSG-00109-001, sent at 18:22:06 — 56 seconds after the meter started at 18:21:10 — reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', and it carries the platform-resolved waypoint for Jurong Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT). The driver accepted it at MSG-00109-002 ('ok can, i wait at the phv pickup point'), and the GPS trace shows the vehicle stationary 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds — well inside POL-RD-04's 200 m proximity test, and your request is the very example the clause gives. POL-RD-04 therefore excludes the detour distance before POL-RD-01 is applied; the whole of the measured excess is that Jurong Point excursion, so no excess over the threshold remains and no deviation survives. I have noted your point that the record stores no separate figure for the excluded leg (amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are null), but that stored re-quote belongs to POL-RD-05 (endpoint relocation), not POL-RD-04, and the exclusion here is answered by the trace itself. For transparency, had the detour not been yours the POL-RD-02 arithmetic would have been charged_total 21.32 less recomputed_fare 13.32 = a refund of 8.00; that refund does not issue, and the fare stands as charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), so no NO_ACTION 'restore' issue arises.\n\nDriver — the same clause that exonerates the detour also compensates you for the distance you drove but did not bill. The fare breakdown charges 9.60 km while the GPS trace records 13.76 km, a shortfall of 4.16 km, above POL-RD-04's 1.0 km trigger. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 4.16 x 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 3.15, well inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. I award you SGD 3.15. Because the case produces this payment, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same figure (POL-GEN-03); it is the amount this ruling moves, not a refund to the rider, and the rider's own charge stands.\n\nOther points raised. POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d of 511, so no repeat pattern is established — no POL-RD-06(b) FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral. POL-RD-09: the fare carries no ERP gantries (empty set, tolls_erp 0.00) and no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, so there is nothing to correct and no billing-integrity referral. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT); its absence is citable and means POL-RD-03 could exonerate nothing, but the exoneration here rests on POL-RD-04, not on any road condition. The rider's argument that the driver must price the whole 115% out of the claim is rejected: the trace and the resolved Jurong Point waypoint show the deviation is the requested excursion. The GPS trace is complete at weight 1.0 (207 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps), the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires. Confidence 0.9 is above the 0.70 floor. No clause-mandated referrals apply."
  },
